      "content": "that's a bit vague lol. i mean, most textbooks focus a lot on the productivity gains and the expansion of markets during that time. is it actually a \"debate\" if the mainstream view is that deregulation was the primary driver for the growth we saw in the 90s? or is the inequality argument just a secondary criticism?",
