      "content": "While textbooks often emphasize the growth and market expansion fueled by deregulation, dismissing the inequality debate is inaccurate. Many economists acknowledge the initial dynamism but argue these gains were not evenly distributed. The growth in the 1990s is multifaceted, with structural reforms, technological change, and deregulation all playing contributing roles, not just one primary driver. Thus, while the growth narrative is strong, the critique of widening disparities remains a central, deeply researched part of the academic conversation.",
