      "content": "Economically, productivity gains and overall GDP growth during that period are often cited as measurable successes directly linked to deregulation. However, modern economic analysis increasingly views inequality not merely as a moral complaint, but as a significant economic problem. High levels of income disparity can dampen long-term aggregate demand and suppress potential future economic growth. Therefore, many economists integrate both efficiency measurements and distributive outcomes into a comprehensive view of economic success.",
